{
  "id": "COMPOUND:33280 - PROTEIN:5782",
  "verbalization": "Sarcotrine A is implicated in the biological pathway leading to DMS-273 through multiple indirect mechanisms. The evidence suggests that Sarcotrine A acts as a target for Raji and Hepatocyte cells, with both of these cell types being targets of (3R)-5,8,9-trimethoxy-2,2-dimethyl-3,4-dihydropyrano[2,3-b]quinolin-3-ol and terbutaline, respectively. These compounds ultimately target DMS-273, indicating a chain of molecular interactions where Sarcotrine A may influence the activity of these intermediaries, which in turn affect DMS-273. The shared target of Raji and Hepatocyte cells by different compounds suggests a potential role for Sarcotrine A in modulating cellular responses that are critical for DMS-273's function. The integration of these pathways highlights the complexity of the relationship, with Sarcotrine A potentially playing a role in the regulation of downstream targets that ultimately interact with DMS-273.",
